invariant: INV-16
file: widemul.h
catches: widemul_runtime_test
reason: widemul_rsa_sp1 inverts its branch, so the private operation runs
  rsa_sign64.c's limbs on the native multiply for every answer but
  WIDEMUL_CONSTANT_TIME, a wiped direction's 0 and WIDEMUL_NOT_STATED
  among them, and the ladder on the decomposition for the one answer that
  states the multiply's timing. Every byte still comes out the same.
  bin/widemul_runtime_test counts the calls into each signer and requires
  the 64-bit one alone under the constant-time answer.

--- old
    if (widemul_native(widemul)) {
        return rsa_sign64_sp1(k, em, sig);
--- new
    if (!widemul_native(widemul)) {
        return rsa_sign64_sp1(k, em, sig);
